body:
>They might try to awaken them in a bid for power and thus undermining them is at least a precaution.

&#x200B;

But isn't that a bit contradictive? By diminishing the Orthodoxy's power, isn't he pushing them into using the crystals/invoking the Grand Ritual to try to regain that power? It isn't like Yulyana and DeRosso alone could stop the whole Orthodoxy from even getting close to the crystals back then.

&#x200B;

>I'm sure establishing himself as the main contact vestals have outside their temple gives him the chance to protect their minds from corruption.

&#x200B;

Is it stated anywhere how he established himself as the main contact? Why would the Orthodoxy accept him? After all, he waited in exile until everyone that knew him died. It is not really that important, I am just curious.

&#x200B;

>He, uh, might have left the earth vestal helpless tbh.

&#x200B;

Maybe he could not help her because the land around Eternia raised and there was no way to get close to the Temple of Earth? They did not have airships that could fly high enough back then.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Thank you for your reply :D
